WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.080 --> 00:00:02.250
(twangy country music)

00:00:02.250 --> 00:00:03.420
- [Narrator] Throughout history,

00:00:03.420 --> 00:00:06.794
we've looked at men as the
stars of the boxing world.

00:00:06.794 --> 00:00:09.980
(rapid thumping)

00:00:09.980 --> 00:00:14.880
But these days, some of the
sport's most promising boxers

00:00:15.740 --> 00:00:17.880
come from a special place in California,

00:00:22.460 --> 00:00:25.873
and they're all teenage girls.

00:00:26.720 --> 00:00:29.000
I'm Zoe Saldana from Bese,

00:00:29.000 --> 00:00:30.890
and I'm teaming up with Great Big Story

00:00:30.890 --> 00:00:33.780
to shine a light on
American Latinx excellence

00:00:33.780 --> 00:00:35.010
around the country.

00:00:40.520 --> 00:00:42.650
While boxing has long been a tradition

00:00:42.650 --> 00:00:45.270
in the Central Valley of California,

00:00:45.270 --> 00:00:46.810
it wasn't until a few years ago

00:00:46.810 --> 00:00:49.900
that girls were allowed
to compete professionally.

00:00:49.900 --> 00:00:52.040
But once the sport was opened up to them,

00:00:52.040 --> 00:00:54.070
not only did girls start competing,

00:00:54.070 --> 00:00:57.310
they started winning a lot.

00:00:57.310 --> 00:01:00.270
In 2017, four girls
from the Central Valley

00:01:00.270 --> 00:01:03.023
finished first or second
at the Junior Olympics.

00:01:04.590 --> 00:01:07.598
- Once you're in that ring,
it's just and your opponent.

00:01:07.598 --> 00:01:08.783
That's it.

00:01:09.650 --> 00:01:11.910
- I keep all my aggressiveness
inside the ring.

00:01:11.910 --> 00:01:13.655
I'm a beast inside the ring.

00:01:13.655 --> 00:01:16.160
(grunting and indistinct yelling)

00:01:16.160 --> 00:01:17.380
- [Sandra] To be the number one spot,

00:01:17.380 --> 00:01:20.310
it takes a lot of hard
work and dedication,

00:01:20.310 --> 00:01:22.103
but it's all worth it in the end.

00:01:24.940 --> 00:01:27.490
- [Narrator] The one leading
the pack is Sandra Tovar,

00:01:27.490 --> 00:01:30.450
who at only 17 is ranked
number one in the nation

00:01:30.450 --> 00:01:32.370
in her weight class.

00:01:32.370 --> 00:01:34.960
She started boxing when
she was only 8 years old

00:01:34.960 --> 00:01:38.073
with her father, who remains
her coach to this day.

00:01:40.100 --> 00:01:43.587
- I train six days a week,
three trainings a day.

00:01:43.587 --> 00:01:46.130
(energetic funk music)

00:01:46.130 --> 00:01:49.160
I wake up in the morning,
and I go to school.

00:01:49.160 --> 00:01:51.430
I do my homework on the way to boxing,

00:01:51.430 --> 00:01:53.080
and I do it on the way back home.

00:01:54.020 --> 00:01:56.230
My biggest goal right now
is to make it to Olympics

00:01:56.230 --> 00:01:57.280
and get a gold medal.

00:01:59.010 --> 00:02:02.135
For me to make that goal possible,

00:02:02.135 --> 00:02:04.900
every single tournament that is coming up,

00:02:04.900 --> 00:02:08.160
I have to win it and
gather up all my points

00:02:08.160 --> 00:02:09.250
for my weight class

00:02:10.460 --> 00:02:11.810
and just keep pushing hard.

00:02:15.620 --> 00:02:17.310
- Keep that jab pumping.

00:02:17.310 --> 00:02:18.620
Relax.

00:02:18.620 --> 00:02:20.870
I've been coaching since 1992,

00:02:20.870 --> 00:02:22.960
and I've trained a lot of champions

00:02:22.960 --> 00:02:25.313
and Sandra stands out.

00:02:27.610 --> 00:02:30.530
I remember when the sport
of boxing was just boys,

00:02:30.530 --> 00:02:33.320
but I believe this new generation of girls

00:02:33.320 --> 00:02:34.423
is gonna change it.

00:02:35.360 --> 00:02:37.930
- [Narrator] Competing
professionally is expensive,

00:02:37.930 --> 00:02:39.360
and it's become a major obstacle

00:02:39.360 --> 00:02:41.570
for many boxers in the Central Valley.

00:02:41.570 --> 00:02:43.670
But thanks to the
community banding together

00:02:43.670 --> 00:02:45.420
to raise funds to send these girls

00:02:45.420 --> 00:02:47.400
to compete at the national level,

00:02:47.400 --> 00:02:49.030
the Central Valley has contributed

00:02:49.030 --> 00:02:50.703
to the changing face of boxing.

00:02:51.990 --> 00:02:54.600
- I believe it's because
of the way they're raised.

00:02:54.600 --> 00:02:56.420
They don't have much,

00:02:56.420 --> 00:02:59.573
and they're willing to do
whatever it takes to move up.

00:03:00.450 --> 00:03:01.970
It makes them hungrier.

00:03:01.970 --> 00:03:04.420
Makes them stronger-willed

00:03:04.420 --> 00:03:06.837
to reach what they wanna get out of life.

00:03:06.837 --> 00:03:07.795
Don't worry about those posts.

00:03:07.795 --> 00:03:08.628
They don't mean nothing.

00:03:08.628 --> 00:03:10.100
I want you to really hurt her.

00:03:10.100 --> 00:03:13.770
- I feel like the spots are
open tremendously right now

00:03:13.770 --> 00:03:15.697
in the sport of female boxing,

00:03:15.697 --> 00:03:18.380
and I feel like it's
gonna end up getting equal

00:03:18.380 --> 00:03:19.878
to men's boxing.

00:03:19.878 --> 00:03:22.628
(tranquil music)

